  "body": "Chrome/Edge seems clear pending error event if img.src changed before it fired.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n``` javascript\nvar image1 = new Image();\nvar image2 = new Image();\n\nimage1.src = '';\nimage2.src = '';\n\nimage1.onerror = function() {\n  console.log('image1.onerror');\n  image2.src = 'data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\"><path d=\"M10,10L32,90L90,32z\" fill=\"lightgreen\"/></svg>';\n};\n\nimage2.onerror = function() {\n  console.log('image2.onerror');\n};\n```\n\nResult of Chrome and Edge:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Image2's error event isn't fired.\n<br>\n**Example 2:**\n\n``` javascript\nvar image1 = new Image();\nvar image2 = new Image();\n\nimage1.src = '';\nimage2.src = '';\n\nimage1.onerror = function() {\n  console.log('image1.onerror');\n  image2.src = '';\n};\n\nimage2.onerror = function() {\n  console.log('image2.onerror');\n};\n```\n\nResult of Chrome and Edge:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Image2's error event is only fired once.\n<br>\nThis behavior (clear pending error event) isn't documented in the [spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#update-the-image-data). But some sites seems rely on this behavior, e.g. https://www.bing.com/mapspreview [1]. Does this behavior is what we expect? \n\n[1] Please also see https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1308069\n",
